cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or its frozen report, please cite it as below. The run
  artifacts are a separate dataset release, listed under references.
type: software
title: "Natural Language Autoencoders for Redundancy Diagnostics: the Answer-Stable Tail"
abstract: >-
  Code, frozen research report and decision record for a study of whether a
  natural-language autoencoder's verbalised readout of layer-20 activations of
  Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct says anything about the answer-stable tail of reasoning
  traces that cheaper signals do not. On 250 GSM8K and MATH problems the
  readout did not beat semantic entropy or a hidden-state probe at matched
  token budget; the causal question (RQ3) was not tested on this model.
